# EtCountryFlag Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtCountryFlag` is a simple, presentational component that renders a country flag SVG by ISO country code. It uses the local SVG flag assets stored in `core/country-flags/svg/`.

**Does:**

- Renders a country flag SVG given an ISO code (e.g., "IL", "US", "GB")
- Displays **circular flags** (36x36px by default) from native circular SVG assets
- Scales the flag based on the `size` prop
- Falls back to a generic placeholder flag (`zz`) for unrecognized ISO codes

**Does NOT:**

- Handle country selection logic
- Fetch flags remotely (all flags are bundled locally)
- Apply any styling beyond sizing

## Visual Design

The component renders a circular flag SVG:

```text
  ╭────╮
 │  🇮🇱  │   36 x 36 px circle (default)
  ╰────╯
```

The `size` prop controls the flag diameter (default: 36px). All flag SVGs are natively circular with `viewBox="0 0 36 36"` and rendered directly without additional clipping.

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtCountryFlag` (main component)

```tsx
<EtCountryFlag
  isoCode: string              // Required - ISO country code (e.g., "IL", "US")
  size?: number                // Circle diameter in px (default: 36)
  testID?: string              // Test identifier
  accessibilityLabel?: string  // Accessibility label (defaults to isoCode)
/>
```

### Types

```typescript
export interface EtCountryFlagProps {
  /** ISO country code (e.g., "IL", "US", "GB") */
  isoCode: string;

  /** Flag circle diameter in pixels. @default 36 */
  size?: number;

  /** Test identifier */
  testID?: string;

  /** Accessibility label (defaults to isoCode if not provided) */
  accessibilityLabel?: string;
}
```

## Usage Patterns

### Basic flag

```tsx
<EtCountryFlag isoCode="IL" />
```

### Custom size

```tsx
<EtCountryFlag isoCode="US" size={56} />
```

### With accessibility

```tsx
<EtCountryFlag isoCode="GB" accessibilityLabel="United Kingdom" testID="user-flag" />
```

## Anti-patterns

### Using lowercase ISO codes

```tsx
// OK - getFlagComponent handles lowercase conversion internally
<EtCountryFlag isoCode="il" />
```

### Expecting remote flag loading

```tsx
// BAD - EtCountryFlag does not fetch remote images
// All flags must exist in core/country-flags/svg/
<EtCountryFlag isoCode="XX" /> // Falls back to 'zz' placeholder flag
```

### Setting width and height separately

```tsx
// BAD - use size prop only, it controls the circle diameter
<EtCountryFlag isoCode="IL" style={{ width: 50, height: 50 }} />
```

**Fix:** Use the `size` prop which controls the circle diameter.

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `getFlagComponent` from `core/country-flags` — resolves ISO code to SVG component
- SVG flag files in `core/country-flags/svg/` — 260 circular country flag SVGs (36x36) from Figma
- `react-native-svg` — SVG rendering (used under the hood by svg-transformer)

### External Dependencies

- `react` — `memo`, `useMemo`

## Patterns & Pitfalls

### Memoized flag lookup

`getFlagComponent(isoCode)` is wrapped in `useMemo` to avoid unnecessary registry lookups on re-renders. The component itself is wrapped in `React.memo` to skip re-renders when props haven't changed.

### Fallback flag (`zz`)

If the ISO code doesn't match any flag in the registry, the component automatically falls back to the `zz` flag — a generic placeholder (question mark icon). This ensures the UI never shows an empty gap. If even the `zz` flag is missing from the registry, the component renders `null` as a last resort.

### Circular rendering

All flag SVGs have `viewBox="0 0 36 36"` and are natively circular. The component renders them directly at the specified `size` without additional clipping or transformations.

